# File storage: Supabase Storage only

All file uploads, downloads, deletes, and signed/public URLs MUST use **Supabase Storage** via `supabase.storage` from `@/lib/supabase/server` (or the browser client when appropriate).

## Forbidden

- `@vercel/blob` (`put`, `del`, `list`, `head`, `copy`)
- Any other object store (S3 SDK direct, Cloudflare R2, Uploadthing, etc.) unless the user explicitly asks
- Storing long-lived public third-party blob URLs as the source of truth for new uploads

## Required

- Create or reuse a named bucket (migration: `INSERT INTO storage.buckets … ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING`)
- Default public app uploads go in **`app-uploads`** via `@/lib/storage/app-uploads` (`uploadAppFile`, `removeStoredPublicUrl`)
- Prefer **private** buckets for anything with PII that must not be world-readable (`letters`, `sir-profiles`); serve via signed URLs or an authenticated download API
- Persist **`storage_path`** (and bucket when not implied) in the DB when using private buckets — not only a public URL
- Check upload/download errors; use upsert only when replacing a known path
- Storage upsert needs INSERT + SELECT + UPDATE policies when RLS applies to non–service-role clients

## Canonical pattern

```typescript
// GOOD — public app uploads
import { buildAppUploadPath, uploadAppFile } from '@/lib/storage/app-uploads';

const path = buildAppUploadPath('register/entry-id', file.name);
const { url } = await uploadAppFile({
  path,
  body: await file.arrayBuffer(),
  contentType: file.type,
});

// GOOD — private (letters / SIR)
import { supabase } from '@/lib/supabase/server';
await supabase.storage.from('letters').upload(storagePath, fileBuffer, {
  contentType: 'application/pdf',
  upsert: true,
});

// BAD
import { put } from '@vercel/blob';
await put(filename, fileBuffer, { access: 'public' });
```

Never add `@vercel/blob` or other object stores. Data still on Blob URLs can be moved with `pnpm storage:migrate-blob`.
